### Shopping Cart API — example requests
### Works with the "REST Client" VS Code extension or any compatible client.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/v1

### Health check (version-neutral)
GET http://localhost:3000/health

### List the product catalog
GET {{baseUrl}}/products

### Get a single product
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/1

### List the available coupons
GET {{baseUrl}}/coupons

### Create a new, empty cart
# @name createCart
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts

### Get a cart by id (replace {{cartId}} with the id returned above)
@cartId = {{createCart.response.body.id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}

### Add a product to the cart (enters with the requested quantity, defaults to 1)
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 2
}

### Add the same product again (sums onto the existing quantity)
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 1
}

### Try to add more than the available stock (treated error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 5,
  "quantity": 999
}

### Set the exact quantity of an existing item
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 5
}

### Remove an item from the cart
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items/1

### Apply a coupon
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/coupon
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "10OFF"
}

### Applying a second coupon replaces the first one (only one active at a time)
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/coupon
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "15OFF"
}

### Applying an unknown coupon returns a treated error
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/coupon
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "DOES-NOT-EXIST"
}

### Remove the applied coupon
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/coupon

### Finalize (checkout) the cart
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/checkout

### Any change attempted after checkout returns a treated error
POST {{baseUrl}}/carts/{{cartId}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 2,
  "quantity": 1
}
